                <pb facs="0817" n="789" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v15/pg789"/>

                <head>433. Memorandum From the Secretary of State’s Special Assistant (Russell) to
                    the Secretary of State<anchor n="1" xml:id="d433-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1956-07-09"><hi rendition="#italic">July 9,
                        1956</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Fawzi Approach to British Ambassador on Israel–Arab Settlement</item>
                </list>
                <p>Mr. Bailey of the British Embassy has just left with me the attached telegrams.
                    One of them, from Trevelyan to the Foreign Office, reports a new approach by
                    Fawzi, authorized by Nasser, to an Israel–Arab settlement. It would be based
                    upon initial conversations by Hammarskjold with both sides, to be followed by
                    final recommendations on the terms of the settlement by a group of outside
                    powers. The second telegram gives the initial reaction of the Foreign
                    Office.</p>
                <p>The Foreign Office intends to cable Trevelyan asking him to express to Fawzi the
                    tentative U.K. views before Nasser leaves for Brioni on July 12. The Foreign
                    Office would like our comments before cabling Trevelyan.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d433-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">F.H.R.</hi></signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d433-a1.xml" xpointer="d433-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d433-a2.xml" xpointer="d433-a2"/>
            </div>
